# macOS Homebrew CASKS — GUI apps + cask-only tools, installed by tools/setup/macos.sh
# (`brew install --cask`). Formulae live in manifests/brew; cross-platform CLIs live in
# .mise.toml. Add a cask by appending a line. Comments start with `#`. Tier tags
# (tier=slim|standard|full) are honored exactly as in manifests/brew.
#
# Why this manifest exists (Aaron 2026-06-21 — "general casks support for mac is good …
# keep it"): casks are a separate brew namespace (`brew install --cask` / `brew list
# --cask`) than formulae, so they need their own declarative list + loop (macos.sh §3b).
# Standing infra for any future mac-only GUI app / cask-only tool.
#
# NOTE on 1Password: the CLI (`op`) is CROSS-OS and lives in .mise.toml (one pinned `op`
# for mac+linux+windows — Aaron: "just the cli … all our oses"), NOT here. The 1Password
# DESKTOP APP is intentionally NOT a dep (CLI + scoped service accounts suffice for agent
# secret access; the app/SSH-agent can be added later if the custody lane needs it).
#
# Format: <cask> [tap=<owner/tap>] [tier=slim|standard|full]
#   tap=<owner/tap> — a custom tap (tapped + trusted before install). Append real casks
#   below as needed; the §3b loop installs them idempotently, tier-gated.

# cvc5 — SMT solver (formal-verification portfolio), distributed via a custom cask tap.
# Migrated 2026-06-21 from a one-off block in macos.sh into this general framework (Aaron:
# "update our special one off cask to use our new general framework too"). The tap= token
# taps + trusts cvc5/cvc5 before the cask install.
cvc5  tap=cvc5/cvc5

# ── YubiHSM 2 SDK (2026-08-20) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aaron, 2026-08-20: "can we save all the yubikey and yubihsm software/drivers i
# installed today as ACE packagemanager missing, we need to make sure new
# contributors to Zeta just get this for free on Mac, Windows, Linux".
#
# THIS ROW CORRECTS A CLAIM I MADE MYSELF. On 2026-08-18 I wrote, in
# docs/research/2026-08-18-yubihsm2-sdk-on-linux-*.md section 6, that "Homebrew
# has no yubihsm-shell and no yubihsm-connector formula (checked against
# formulae.brew.sh -- both 404)" and concluded no clean macOS route existed. The
# 404s were real and are still real (re-checked today: both formulae 404). The
# conclusion was wrong, because I checked the FORMULA namespace and the SDK is
# packaged as a CASK. That is the same error the manifests/apt block records
# against itself one manifest over -- verifying the weaker proposition and
# treating it as the stronger one -- committed by the person who wrote that
# warning. Recorded rather than quietly fixed.
#
# Verified 2026-08-20 against the Homebrew API, not from memory:
#   https://formulae.brew.sh/api/cask/yubihsm2-sdk.json
#   token yubihsm2-sdk | tap homebrew/cask | version 2026-04 | Apache-2.0 upstream
#   arm64  yubihsm2-sdk-2026-04-darwin-arm64.pkg  sha256 2f8e80e9...9e0612  (15,361,954 bytes)
#   amd64  yubihsm2-sdk-2026-04-darwin-amd64.pkg  sha256 89d22782...2cca59
#   artifact: pkg + uninstall pkgutil com.yubico.yubihsm2-sdk
#
# WHY THIS AND NOT from-url. from-url would need a hand-supplied sha256 and could
# only DOWNLOAD the .pkg -- its realizer fetches to a path and stops; nothing in
# it runs `installer -pkg`. The cask carries the digest upstream (maintained in a
# public repo with history, so it is a pin somebody else also has to defend) AND
# performs the pkg install AND registers an uninstall receipt. Same vendor bytes,
# a digest we did not invent, an existing mechanism. No new mechanism was needed.
#
# WHAT IT INSTALLS, and why it is exactly the hand-install being replaced: the
# .pkg writes /usr/local, which is why the working copy on the maintainer's host
# is /usr/local/bin/yubihsm-shell + /usr/local/bin/yubihsm-connector rather than
# /opt/homebrew/bin. The PKCS#11 module lands at
# /usr/local/lib/pkcs11/yubihsm_pkcs11.dylib -- measured on the attached device
# 2026-08-18 (Q8 in the design doc), so the path contract here is verified, not
# assumed.
#
# NOT tier-gated, deliberately. A tier= token would make macos-install-sh-test
# (a 7 GB runner, so slim/standard) skip the row, and a row CI never exercises is
# a check that did not run wearing the face of one that passed. Un-gated, the
# macOS install shield actually proves the cask installs. Cost: one 15 MB
# download on macos-install-sh-test, which is path-filtered to tools/setup/** and
# .mise.toml -- not on the 24 gate jobs. The shield's 2nd (idempotency) run hits
# `brew list --cask` -> `brew upgrade --cask`, a metadata check, not a re-download.
#
# SUDO: a `pkg` cask artifact runs `sudo installer -pkg ... -target /`. That is
# not new to this script -- common/fd-limits.sh already runs `sudo sysctl` on the
# macOS path and the shield is green with it -- but it is the reason a contributor
# running macos.sh may be prompted for a password at this step. Named so it is a
# known behaviour and not a surprise.
yubihsm2-sdk   # YubiHSM 2 SDK — yubihsm-shell, yubihsm-connector, yubihsm-setup, yubihsm_pkcs11.dylib
